WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.990 --> 00:00:12.340
Welcome to Looper.

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.700
I'm Brian Rubin.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:17.039
Today, we're talking all about the Marvel
Cinematic Universe.

00:00:17.039 --> 00:00:23.930
You know, the MCU has brought us some legendary
villains over the last 10 years or so: Agatha

00:00:23.930 --> 00:00:28.340
Harkness, Killmonger, and of course, the big
purple guy, Thanos.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:34.320
The MCU has also brought us some less legendary
bad guys, guys like Yellowjacket, Malekith,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.960
and Garry Shandling.

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:40.440
I'm joined today by Tom and Nina to try and
answer the question, who are the best and

00:00:40.440 --> 00:00:44.460
worst villains the Marvel Cinematic Universe
could introduce in phase four.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.540
Tom, Nina, hello.

00:00:45.540 --> 00:00:46.980
Hey, how are you?

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:47.980
Hi.

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:48.980
Good.

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:52.420
Are you implying that Garry Shandling [inaudible]
of us?

00:00:52.420 --> 00:01:01.780
I'm just saying that as far as a villain is
concerned, not the top tier bad guy kind of

00:01:01.780 --> 00:01:02.780
thing.

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:03.780
No.

00:01:03.780 --> 00:01:07.439
I love Garry Shandling, but is he...

00:01:07.439 --> 00:01:09.063
Anyway, you know what I'm saying.

00:01:09.063 --> 00:01:11.820
I don't know, did you ever see Mixed Nuts?

00:01:11.820 --> 00:01:14.990
That's in darkness, man.

00:01:14.990 --> 00:01:16.270
Rest in peace [inaudible].

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:21.020
So Tom-
Who are the best and worst villains that Marvel

00:01:21.020 --> 00:01:22.490
could introduce in phase four?

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:25.799
I'm glad that you asked that, Brian, because
I was thinking about this just the other night

00:01:25.799 --> 00:01:27.420
while I was writing down ideas-
That's so weird.

00:01:27.420 --> 00:01:29.200
... because you told me to.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.200
Yeah.

00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:34.390
Who are the best and worst villains that we
can bring back into the MC?

00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:38.869
Personally, I think in terms of the best villain...

00:01:38.869 --> 00:01:39.869
What makes a good villain?

00:01:39.869 --> 00:01:41.500
Is there an objective answer?

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:43.899
But Vincent D'Onofrio from Daredevil.

00:01:43.899 --> 00:01:46.560
That would be my number one top pick.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.920
If we could bring one guy back, the intensity
that that guy brought to the role, just spectacular,

00:01:50.920 --> 00:01:52.299
practically alien.

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:53.340
So weird and creepy.

00:01:53.340 --> 00:01:54.640
I love the guy.

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:58.930
You're thinking about villains that could
come back into the MCU, is that where we're

00:01:58.930 --> 00:01:59.930
going?

00:01:59.930 --> 00:02:00.930
I don't know.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:07.090
Have we determined whether or not we're [inaudible]
Netflix as stuff that happened in the MC Universe?

00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:08.090
That's a good point.

00:02:08.090 --> 00:02:09.959
Netflix is definitely stuff that happened.

00:02:09.959 --> 00:02:15.280
My particular question here was what villains
could they bring into the MCU from the comics?

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.260
But I think it's totally valid to ask what
villains that we've had before could come

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:20.860
back too.

00:02:20.860 --> 00:02:24.120
All villains are on the table as long as they
are Marvel villains.

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:25.120
Got it.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:30.560
So in terms of fresh to the MCU, at a very
personal level, I would love to see Sentinels

00:02:30.560 --> 00:02:32.670
pop up at some point.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:37.970
Those were one of the first terrifying nightmares
that I remember having as a kid.

00:02:37.970 --> 00:02:41.360
It was those big purple that get the things.

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:47.980
Before I die, I would love to see Sentinels
done right on the big screen, just like giant,

00:02:47.980 --> 00:02:51.000
terrifying, [crosstalk] monsters.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.920
Are you in favor of a Master Mold, perhaps?

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:55.360
I don't know if it's dark and raised.

00:02:55.360 --> 00:02:57.490
I'd say go get it checked out.

00:02:57.490 --> 00:03:00.970
But you know, man.

00:03:00.970 --> 00:03:07.160
Master Mold, of course, is the giant mama
Sentinel that makes the big Sentinels, but

00:03:07.160 --> 00:03:09.230
they're it's baby Sentinels.

00:03:09.230 --> 00:03:11.670
Master Mold is a classic X-Men villain.

00:03:11.670 --> 00:03:14.850
Don't talk to me like I'm people that don't
know Master Mold.

00:03:14.850 --> 00:03:16.520
I know you know Master Mold.

00:03:16.520 --> 00:03:18.921
I'm trying to explain who Master Mold might
be.

00:03:18.921 --> 00:03:20.650
We're trying to translate, Tom.

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:21.650
Yes.

00:03:21.650 --> 00:03:23.270
Anyway, you want to see the Sentinels.

00:03:23.270 --> 00:03:24.620
You want to see Vincent D'Onofrio.

00:03:24.620 --> 00:03:27.460
Tell us more about the villains you'd like
to see.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:32.500
My only other big thing is there's a caveat
and I'd like to come back around to it in

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:33.500
a minute.

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:36.540
I feel like we've got to see Galactus at some
point, right?

00:03:36.540 --> 00:03:37.540
Yes.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:38.830
I think so, yeah.

00:03:38.830 --> 00:03:45.870
It's one of the last really big, recognizable
way over the top villains that Marvel hasn't

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.800
really touched too much.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:54.360
We know that they haven't been able to touch
Galactus because up until very recently, Galactus,

00:03:54.360 --> 00:03:59.270
as a member of the Fantastic Four cast of
characters, he's a Fantastic Four villain

00:03:59.270 --> 00:04:03.970
first and foremost, Marvel Studios hasn't
had the rights to use Galactus because they

00:04:03.970 --> 00:04:05.050
were owned by Fox.

00:04:05.050 --> 00:04:10.420
Now Marvel Disney owns Fox, and so that opens
things up for guys like the Sentinels who

00:04:10.420 --> 00:04:13.930
were also X-Men, also owned by Fox for the
movie rights.

00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:19.259
Now Sentinels, now Galactus are both available
to come into the Marvel Universe.

00:04:19.259 --> 00:04:21.079
I 100% agree.

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:22.470
Galactus was on my list that...

00:04:22.470 --> 00:04:28.620
You can see he's right there above my head,
watching over all of us, Galactus, my friend,

00:04:28.620 --> 00:04:29.620
my best friend.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:30.689
I like to think he always is.

00:04:30.689 --> 00:04:31.689
Yeah.

00:04:31.689 --> 00:04:32.689
Yeah.

00:04:32.689 --> 00:04:35.949
Tom, do you want to explain who Galactus is
and just what his deal is?

00:04:35.949 --> 00:04:38.159
I'm glad that you ask, Brian.

00:04:38.159 --> 00:04:41.909
You know the song, Food, Glorious Food from
the Oliver musical?

00:04:41.909 --> 00:04:43.819
He's that, but he's a person.

00:04:43.819 --> 00:04:50.979
He is a semi timeless entity from a universe
that...

00:04:50.979 --> 00:04:53.840
They get destroyed before ours was ever created.

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:57.819
He's all that's left of this other universe
and he loves eating planets, man.

00:04:57.819 --> 00:04:58.819
He's all about eating planet.

00:04:58.819 --> 00:04:59.819
He loves two things.

00:04:59.819 --> 00:05:03.900
He loves a good helmet and he loves a delicious
planet sandwich.

00:05:03.900 --> 00:05:07.099
I love how his helmet has a little brim on
it on the front end-

00:05:07.099 --> 00:05:08.099
It does.

00:05:08.099 --> 00:05:09.099
... like a little baseball cap.

00:05:09.099 --> 00:05:10.099
But why?

00:05:10.099 --> 00:05:14.210
I also like the little mask.

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:17.210
I think that's my favorite part is he's got
the little domino mask-

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:18.860
Just a little domino mask.

00:05:18.860 --> 00:05:21.330
... scoped into it just to protect his identity.

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:23.889
[crosstalk]
His original design, he had a big belt with

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:25.560
a G on it and bike shorts.

00:05:25.560 --> 00:05:26.730
Yeah, he did.

00:05:26.730 --> 00:05:27.900
In short shorts.

00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:28.900
Nice.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:31.789
Bike shorts, they're making a comeback, so
that could work.

00:05:31.789 --> 00:05:37.419
They're all the rage out in the outer reaches
of space.

00:05:37.419 --> 00:05:38.779
Yeah.

00:05:38.779 --> 00:05:41.490
You would know this if you ever watched [inaudible].

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:42.490
True.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:47.699
Did you have any other villains for your list,
Tom?

00:05:47.699 --> 00:05:49.810
Not for the best ones, no.

00:05:49.810 --> 00:05:50.810
Okay.

00:05:50.810 --> 00:05:56.650
Nina, what about your best villain that the
MCU could bring in in phase four?

00:05:56.650 --> 00:06:00.479
I've only got the one and while I was doing
research for this, I stumbled on her.

00:06:00.479 --> 00:06:03.009
I wasn't that familiar, so I did some research
at...

00:06:03.009 --> 00:06:09.030
I stumbled upon Amora, also known as the Enchantress,
who is a Thor villain.

00:06:09.030 --> 00:06:10.030
Yes.

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:11.030
And she is cool.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:13.289
I really loved Cate Blanchett's Hela.

00:06:13.289 --> 00:06:17.969
I really love a good female antagonist and
she sounds awesome.

00:06:17.969 --> 00:06:24.309
I think that having Chris Hemsworth have a
really seductive villain to play off of could

00:06:24.309 --> 00:06:29.090
be tremendously fun, especially if Taika Waititi
keeps directing Thor movies.

00:06:29.090 --> 00:06:34.500
I have the worst news, Nina.

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.949
They did that on Agents of Shield.

00:06:36.949 --> 00:06:38.449
Didn't they bring her in in Agents of Shield?

00:06:38.449 --> 00:06:41.110
Oh, I didn't-
Was she Enchantress on Agents of Shield?

00:06:41.110 --> 00:06:45.199
I think she was in Agents of Shield but she
got the whole like Power Rangers treatment

00:06:45.199 --> 00:06:47.479
that that show gave to so many of its characters.

00:06:47.479 --> 00:06:49.689
No, I don't think you're right.

00:06:49.689 --> 00:06:50.940
I could be wrong.

00:06:50.940 --> 00:06:51.940
We're going to look this up in a few minutes.

00:06:51.940 --> 00:06:53.430
I would love to be wrong.

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:56.659
I think it was a different-
Please be wrong because I was really jazzed

00:06:56.659 --> 00:06:57.659
about this.

00:06:57.659 --> 00:06:58.659
I know.

00:06:58.659 --> 00:06:59.659
I hate disappointing Nina.

00:06:59.659 --> 00:07:05.569
I think it's a different character from the
comics that was Enchantress adjacent, if I

00:07:05.569 --> 00:07:10.499
recall correctly, I will admit it's been a
long time since I've watched Agents of Shield.

00:07:10.499 --> 00:07:11.499
Same.

00:07:11.499 --> 00:07:13.910
I will also admit I didn't finish Agents of
Shield.

00:07:13.910 --> 00:07:15.060
Nobody did, man.

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:16.060
Same.

00:07:16.060 --> 00:07:18.180
[crosstalk] couldn't finish Agents of Shield.

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:19.509
Yeah.

00:07:19.509 --> 00:07:25.050
I got forgot that it was a show, to be honest,
until right now when you said Agents of Shield.

00:07:25.050 --> 00:07:26.819
I'm really sorry.

00:07:26.819 --> 00:07:27.819
Yeah.

00:07:27.819 --> 00:07:32.319
I'm almost positive it was a different character
that wasn't quite the Enchantress, but she

00:07:32.319 --> 00:07:34.490
did basically everything the Enchantress did.

00:07:34.490 --> 00:07:37.080
But with that said-
I want to believe you.

00:07:37.080 --> 00:07:38.860
... but let's also be real here though.

00:07:38.860 --> 00:07:42.520
Even if Agents of Shield did do that, they
also did the Inhumans and then they made an

00:07:42.520 --> 00:07:43.740
Inhuman show anyway-
Right.

00:07:43.740 --> 00:07:44.740
That's true.

00:07:44.740 --> 00:07:47.419
... that was totally different and divorced
from everything happening [crosstalk].

00:07:47.419 --> 00:07:48.419
Right.

00:07:48.419 --> 00:07:50.650
And if we're talking Vincent D'Onofrio, then
we can talk the Enchantress too.

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:51.650
I think that's fair game.

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:52.650
Totally fair.

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:54.800
They could just say it was a different Enchantress.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:56.870
It was a different incarnation of the Enchantress-
Right.

00:07:56.870 --> 00:07:59.819
... if they even acknowledge that it happened
on Agents of Shield at all.

00:07:59.819 --> 00:08:01.339
So far, the only acknowledgement-
True.

00:08:01.339 --> 00:08:05.960
... of anything that happened on Agents of
Shield in the movies was the inclusion of

00:08:05.960 --> 00:08:08.680
TV Jarvis from the Peggy [coast].

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:09.680
Oh, yeah.

00:08:09.680 --> 00:08:10.680
Oh, right.

00:08:10.680 --> 00:08:11.680
That's it.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:12.680
Yeah.

00:08:12.680 --> 00:08:13.680
Because he's great.

00:08:13.680 --> 00:08:14.680
That's true.

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:15.680
That's true.

00:08:15.680 --> 00:08:16.999
So there's room for Enchantress.

00:08:16.999 --> 00:08:17.999
I love the Enchantress.

00:08:17.999 --> 00:08:18.999
She's a great villain.

00:08:18.999 --> 00:08:20.199
She's great, yeah.

00:08:20.199 --> 00:08:25.360
Reading more about her, I was trying to think
of who would play her?

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:30.430
Just trying to, maybe not the right age, but
a Laura Dern-type would be really fun and

00:08:30.430 --> 00:08:31.460
campy in that role.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:33.070
Laura Dern would be great.

00:08:33.070 --> 00:08:34.070
Yeah.

00:08:34.070 --> 00:08:35.610
My mind went to January Jones.

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:39.570
Your mind always goes to January.

00:08:39.570 --> 00:08:41.610
No, that's good.

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:42.850
Every month of the year.

00:08:42.850 --> 00:08:46.430
When she's given room to play around in a
role like on Last Man on Earth, she really

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:47.430
have a good time.

00:08:47.430 --> 00:08:48.430
Yes.

00:08:48.430 --> 00:08:49.430
That would be fun.

00:08:49.430 --> 00:08:50.430
She's so fun.

00:08:50.430 --> 00:08:51.430
She's so good.

00:08:51.430 --> 00:08:54.620
If she's allowed to let loose and just be
weird and fun, she could be amazing.

00:08:54.620 --> 00:08:55.620
Yes.

00:08:55.620 --> 00:09:00.410
She wasn't very good as Emma Frost, but no
one was good in that movie, which was...

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:01.410
Right.

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:02.410
Which movie was that?

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:03.410
No, that was First Class.

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.410
That was First class.

00:09:04.410 --> 00:09:05.410
First Class, yeah.

00:09:05.410 --> 00:09:06.410
Let me back up.

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:08.220
Some people were good in that movie.

00:09:08.220 --> 00:09:09.920
I do think-
[crosstalk] really have much to do besides

00:09:09.920 --> 00:09:12.079
that [inaudible], now we're close.

00:09:12.079 --> 00:09:13.430
Yes, that's true.

00:09:13.430 --> 00:09:14.430
Right.

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:17.190
I'm going to walk back my statement slagging
off all of First Class.

00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:18.190
Yes.

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:19.910
It was some good-
I'm going to fan cast and [inaudible] too.

00:09:19.910 --> 00:09:22.500
I'm going to pick January Jones with an assist
from you.

00:09:22.500 --> 00:09:23.500
Yes.

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:24.500
I'm going to say her.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:25.500
You've got it.

00:09:25.500 --> 00:09:26.500
It's yours.

00:09:26.500 --> 00:09:27.980
She's as good as cast.

00:09:27.980 --> 00:09:28.980
Perfect.

00:09:28.980 --> 00:09:31.050
Somebody call Marvel.

00:09:31.050 --> 00:09:35.250
Whoever plays her, as long as she keeps the
same pants that she had back in the day.

00:09:35.250 --> 00:09:40.000
I want you to create her original costume,
the best pant.

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:44.630
We can go on and on about Galactus' pants,
Enchantress' pants, unbelievable.

00:09:44.630 --> 00:09:49.820
She had very fancy green pants and [crosstalk]
She had the fanciest pants.

00:09:49.820 --> 00:09:51.959
They have a loopy zone.

00:09:51.959 --> 00:10:00.000
So my pick, not that either of you ask, is-
We didn't.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:04.769
I came armed with two because I thought someone
might say one of them and I was right.

00:10:04.769 --> 00:10:06.350
So Tom said Galactus.

00:10:06.350 --> 00:10:14.690
My pick is Doctor Doom who up until now, also
was a Fantastic Four villain, so off limits

00:10:14.690 --> 00:10:19.980
to Marvel Studios, has appeared in two different
iterations of the Fantastic Four franchise.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:23.990
Both times, not the best.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:26.279
But walk these words back, man.

00:10:26.279 --> 00:10:27.759
Let's not say things that we can't take back.

00:10:27.759 --> 00:10:32.790
You're a big fan of the depiction of Doctor
Doom in one of the previous Fantastic Four

00:10:32.790 --> 00:10:34.860
movies?

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:35.860
You know what?

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:36.860
This is a me thing.

00:10:36.860 --> 00:10:37.860
I don't want to bring me things into...

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:43.660
I don't hate the first two, the ones from
the mid-2000s.

00:10:43.660 --> 00:10:46.610
They're not great.

00:10:46.610 --> 00:10:47.740
I'm not going to say good.

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:49.720
I'm not going to say good, but cute, enjoyable.

00:10:49.720 --> 00:10:51.589
So you're not going to backfire, you're just
going to-

00:10:51.589 --> 00:10:53.520
No!
... lightly defend.

00:10:53.520 --> 00:11:00.040
I'm going to prod at defending the story,
Fantastic Four's.

00:11:00.040 --> 00:11:06.019
My issue with the Doctor Doom realization
in those movies specifically, is that it's

00:11:06.019 --> 00:11:12.139
only a fraction of the kind of great stuff
you can do with a guy like Doctor Doom.

00:11:12.139 --> 00:11:14.009
Totally.

00:11:14.009 --> 00:11:17.690
Even if the actor portraying him did a good
job with the material, and there are definitely

00:11:17.690 --> 00:11:21.820
things in those two Fantastic Four movies,
and even though the Josh Trank one, there's

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:24.130
stuff in those movies that I think are cool.

00:11:24.130 --> 00:11:25.130
They're good.

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:26.130
They're interesting.

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:29.589
Chris Evans is, as the Human Torch, was actually
really excellent.

00:11:29.589 --> 00:11:32.319
When he was cast as Captain America, I was
like, "That's great.

00:11:32.319 --> 00:11:33.690
This guy can act.

00:11:33.690 --> 00:11:34.769
He's awesome."

00:11:34.769 --> 00:11:44.100
So Doctor Doom, that actor whose name escapes
me, he's fine for that movie, but overall,

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:54.430
what I want out of a Doctor Doom is a totally
ego maniacal Machiavellian ruler of a European

00:11:54.430 --> 00:12:00.190
country named Latveria that's always weirdly
stuck in the dark ages and always all the

00:12:00.190 --> 00:12:03.470
villagers have pitchforks and torches at any
moment.

00:12:03.470 --> 00:12:06.319
What is with that?

00:12:06.319 --> 00:12:07.319
That's what it looks like there.

00:12:07.319 --> 00:12:08.319
No way.

00:12:08.319 --> 00:12:09.319
That's just what it is.

00:12:09.319 --> 00:12:10.370
I never thought about that.

00:12:10.370 --> 00:12:11.680
But yeah, no, you're right.

00:12:11.680 --> 00:12:15.240
The villagers always look like they're stuck
in the medieval caste system.

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:16.240
That's what he likes.

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:20.949
Do they also have robots that are indiscernible
from living beings?

00:12:20.949 --> 00:12:21.949
Yeah.

00:12:21.949 --> 00:12:26.720
He has a whole army of Doombots that are just...

00:12:26.720 --> 00:12:30.600
Marvel Comics has made an industry out of
explaining a way inconsistencies with his

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:34.560
character by saying, "Oh, that was a Doombot
that thought it was the real Doctor Doom.

00:12:34.560 --> 00:12:37.470
I'm the real Doctor Doom."

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:38.740
So there's so much room for mistakes.

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:39.740
Exactly.

00:12:39.740 --> 00:12:43.020
You can do whatever you want and then [crosstalk]
And this is the character that you want to

00:12:43.020 --> 00:12:46.279
bring in into the MC Universe.

00:12:46.279 --> 00:12:51.959
[crosstalk]
What I like about him is that he is so purely

00:12:51.959 --> 00:12:56.650
and deliciously into his thing.

00:12:56.650 --> 00:13:00.889
He's the hero of his own story and he is the
most heroic hero.

00:13:00.889 --> 00:13:05.960
He has what's called main character syndrome,
where you're like, "I am the protagonist."

00:13:05.960 --> 00:13:08.209
Yeah, [crosstalk]
Yeah.

00:13:08.209 --> 00:13:10.779
Whenever Doctor Doom shows up, the story gets
better.

00:13:10.779 --> 00:13:15.120
Whenever the heroes have to fight Doctor Doom,
it's a great story.

00:13:15.120 --> 00:13:19.009
It doesn't matter what Doctor Doom is doing,
he's just fun.

00:13:19.009 --> 00:13:21.700
He just improves the material.

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.370
He's just so great.

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:28.240
I just love the way he refers to himself in
the third person.

00:13:28.240 --> 00:13:32.490
Again, these are things that don't necessarily
have to come to the movie, but I do think

00:13:32.490 --> 00:13:38.180
that if you can make a guy like Iron Man believable
and interesting and entertaining, you can

00:13:38.180 --> 00:13:41.990
make a guy like Doctor Doom threatening and
yet still entertaining.

00:13:41.990 --> 00:13:49.360
He can have that charisma, that ego, and still
be a menacing bad guy.

00:13:49.360 --> 00:13:51.430
If anyone can do it, Marvel Studios can do
it.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:52.430
So I want Doctor Doom.

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:56.390
So who do you want playing Doctor Doom?

00:13:56.390 --> 00:13:59.269
Who has that level of charisma?

00:13:59.269 --> 00:14:05.720
I saw somebody fan cast, Giancarlo Esposito,
and I thought that that was pretty spot on.

00:14:05.720 --> 00:14:06.720
That's pretty good.

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:07.720
That would be fun.

00:14:07.720 --> 00:14:08.720
That would actually be fantastic.

00:14:08.720 --> 00:14:12.089
I don't know if he wants to spend his entire
life playing enigmatic, largely silent villains,

00:14:12.089 --> 00:14:13.413
but if he does, he will be terrific at that.

00:14:13.413 --> 00:14:16.379
I think that's kind of his thing, yeah.

00:14:16.379 --> 00:14:17.670
But that's a perfect cast.

00:14:17.670 --> 00:14:21.519
I didn't have an answer ready, but as soon
as you said that, I was like, "Yeah, that'll

00:14:21.519 --> 00:14:22.519
work."

00:14:22.519 --> 00:14:23.519
Yeah.

00:14:23.519 --> 00:14:24.519
That would be great.

00:14:24.519 --> 00:14:25.519
No, I think he'd be great.

00:14:25.519 --> 00:14:26.519
I'd pay big money for that.

00:14:26.519 --> 00:14:27.790
Who has the charisma to play Galactus?

00:14:27.790 --> 00:14:30.589
We never got around to that.

00:14:30.589 --> 00:14:31.589
Another good question.

00:14:31.589 --> 00:14:35.720
I wish I'd thought of the casting aspect of
this.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:37.790
Who has the charisma to play Galactus?

00:14:37.790 --> 00:14:41.819
That's what I'm asking you, Brian.

00:14:41.819 --> 00:14:43.209
How funny is Galactus?

00:14:43.209 --> 00:14:44.209
Is he funny?

00:14:44.209 --> 00:14:45.209
No.

00:14:45.209 --> 00:14:46.209
No, he's a hoot.

00:14:46.209 --> 00:14:50.990
He's always like, "Oh, I'm hungry."

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:52.930
He's very pretentious.

00:14:52.930 --> 00:14:54.970
He's always very...

00:14:54.970 --> 00:14:55.970
Gosh.

00:14:55.970 --> 00:14:59.970
That's the kind of question that's really
difficult to answer because if you had said,

00:14:59.970 --> 00:15:05.399
"Who should play Thanos?" we never would have
said, "Josh Brolin."

00:15:05.399 --> 00:15:07.990
No, it's true.

00:15:07.990 --> 00:15:08.990
Right.

00:15:08.990 --> 00:15:09.990
It's an insane answer.

00:15:09.990 --> 00:15:13.720
Frankly, the Thanos that we got in the movies
is pretty different from the Thanos from the

00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:14.720
comics.

00:15:14.720 --> 00:15:15.720
That's a good point.

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:18.470
Obviously, whatever they do with him, they'll
do something good.

00:15:18.470 --> 00:15:22.800
Part of me wants to say Josh Brolin, because
he's already been a great Thanos, so he'd

00:15:22.800 --> 00:15:25.259
probably do a great Galactus, but that would
be silly.

00:15:25.259 --> 00:15:26.360
What about John Cena?

00:15:26.360 --> 00:15:27.360
Sure, why not?

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:28.360
Oh, spectacular.

00:15:28.360 --> 00:15:29.360
Just give it to The Rock.

00:15:29.360 --> 00:15:30.680
Let The Rock.

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:31.680
Yeah.

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:33.379
Let The Rock play all of them.

00:15:33.379 --> 00:15:35.389
Can you smell what Galactus is cooking?

00:15:35.389 --> 00:15:36.389
It's [crosstalk].

00:15:36.389 --> 00:15:38.079
[crosstalk], because he's so hungry.

00:15:38.079 --> 00:15:39.860
Because he's hungry, yeah.

00:15:39.860 --> 00:15:40.860
Love this.

00:15:40.860 --> 00:15:41.899
I think that's the answer.

00:15:41.899 --> 00:15:43.720
I think we've come up with it.

00:15:43.720 --> 00:15:50.790
Who would be the worst villains that Marvel
could bring into MCU phase four?

00:15:50.790 --> 00:15:51.800
Nina.

00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:53.930
I have two.

00:15:53.930 --> 00:16:03.880
One of them is Egghead, a character I didn't
know existed, who is just like a quiet, dweeby

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:07.560
person who is from the Ant-Man comics.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:11.509
I believe he gets murdered pretty quickly
by Hawkeye.

00:16:11.509 --> 00:16:13.639
Let's not bury the lead, Nina.

00:16:13.639 --> 00:16:17.290
What does his head look like?

00:16:17.290 --> 00:16:18.910
He's just called Egghead because he likes
studying.

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:19.910
That's it.

00:16:19.910 --> 00:16:20.910
That's not even a good name.

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:25.149
He has a normal head.

00:16:25.149 --> 00:16:31.610
Then the other one I found which is just horrifying
is Carlos Cabrera or Gamecock, who is a chicken

00:16:31.610 --> 00:16:33.389
man that fights Captain America.

00:16:33.389 --> 00:16:34.610
Shut your mouth.

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:35.610
What?

00:16:35.610 --> 00:16:36.610
You know it's real.

00:16:36.610 --> 00:16:38.720
How do I not know about this?

00:16:38.720 --> 00:16:39.720
I don't know.

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:45.079
He is a minor antagonist in the Captain America
comics.

00:16:45.079 --> 00:16:46.710
His name is Gamecock and he's a chicken man.

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:47.710
Gamecock.

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:50.629
I can say it seems unlikely that they're going
to bring Gamecock.

00:16:50.629 --> 00:16:52.100
I really hope so.

00:16:52.100 --> 00:16:57.389
It seems unlikely that they're going to bring
Batroc the Leaper into this either, but here

00:16:57.389 --> 00:16:58.389
we are.

00:16:58.389 --> 00:16:59.389
Yeah.

00:16:59.389 --> 00:17:00.389
I guess you're right.

00:17:00.389 --> 00:17:02.339
So don't count out Gamecock.

00:17:02.339 --> 00:17:03.499
I don't want to say that.

00:17:03.499 --> 00:17:07.370
I would prefer to count it out.

00:17:07.370 --> 00:17:08.370
I went looking.

00:17:08.370 --> 00:17:11.530
I went poking through marvel.com and all this
stuff and I just saw chicken man and I was

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:13.900
like, "That can't be good."

00:17:13.900 --> 00:17:18.689
I did some research and yeah, in fact, he
is a chicken man.

00:17:18.689 --> 00:17:21.140
He fights Captain America unsuccessfully a
couple of times.

00:17:21.140 --> 00:17:23.380
I don't want to see any part of that.

00:17:23.380 --> 00:17:26.199
I don't want to see a Falcon-Chicken fight.

00:17:26.199 --> 00:17:27.850
He didn't win?

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:29.779
Yeah, no.

00:17:29.779 --> 00:17:34.270
In a shocking turn of events, the chicken
man didn't beat America's superhero.

00:17:34.270 --> 00:17:35.270
I know it's weird.

00:17:35.270 --> 00:17:40.800
You're telling me the chicken dude tried to
fight the leader of the Avenger?

00:17:40.800 --> 00:17:43.030
That didn't pan out.

00:17:43.030 --> 00:17:44.250
Did not end well for him.

00:17:44.250 --> 00:17:46.909
[Crosstalk]
[crosstalk], son of a gun.

00:17:46.909 --> 00:17:48.150
So those are my picks.

00:17:48.150 --> 00:17:49.820
I feel pretty good about them.

00:17:49.820 --> 00:17:50.850
Tom, who would be-
Yes.

00:17:50.850 --> 00:17:56.820
... your worst villain to add to the MCU phase
four?

00:17:56.820 --> 00:18:00.670
I'm going to make a difficult call here.

00:18:00.670 --> 00:18:01.850
Okay.

00:18:01.850 --> 00:18:03.030
Galactus.

00:18:03.030 --> 00:18:04.549
Okay, please explain.

00:18:04.549 --> 00:18:07.240
You got to understand I-
You just hurt Brian's feelings.

00:18:07.240 --> 00:18:08.630
Hey, I hurt my feelings too.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:10.000
I'm so excited to see Galactus.

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:11.000
I would love to see Galactus.

00:18:11.000 --> 00:18:13.230
He was on my list of the best characters to
bring in.

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:17.210
The problem that I think we're going to run
into at this point is that we're running out

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:22.710
of recognizable, back in the day comic book
characters.

00:18:22.710 --> 00:18:24.559
You know what I mean?

00:18:24.559 --> 00:18:29.450
We're down to like half of the original Avengers,
maybe two out of six, something like that.

00:18:29.450 --> 00:18:32.490
Something like that, yeah.

00:18:32.490 --> 00:18:36.790
I don't know if it's going to have the same
gravitas if you'd bring in great, big, bucket-headed,

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:44.700
planet-eater guy, and then the only people
that you have left to fight in my way, White

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:47.420
Vision,-
Well, don't forget.

00:18:47.420 --> 00:18:49.120
Now, hang on though.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:50.120
Winter Soldier.

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:53.220
I'm going to subvert this though.

00:18:53.220 --> 00:18:54.220
By all means.

00:18:54.220 --> 00:18:56.470
Galactus doesn't have to just fight the Avengers.

00:18:56.470 --> 00:18:58.000
Galactus is a Fantastic Four villain.

00:18:58.000 --> 00:18:59.000
He certainly is.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:19:02.620
We know a Fantastic Four movie at the end
of phase four.

00:19:02.620 --> 00:19:07.460
So if you tell me that you're going to introduce
a Fantastic Four movie and then at the end

00:19:07.460 --> 00:19:13.890
of that movie, you don't have a tease for
Galactus is coming and that's our big arc

00:19:13.890 --> 00:19:17.880
over the next several years to prepare for
the coming of Galactus-

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:21.520
I would love to believe that you're right,
Brian, but at the same time, we sat through

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:27.549
all Wanda Vision and at the end, what that
was leading to was [crosstalk].

00:19:27.549 --> 00:19:29.690
She was reading.

00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:30.690
Yeah.

00:19:30.690 --> 00:19:33.820
RIP Ralph Bohner, gone but not forgotten.

00:19:33.820 --> 00:19:38.890
I do feel a little bit like maybe, Kevin's
messing with us now.

00:19:38.890 --> 00:19:43.429
Maybe he got through the main story that he
wanted to tell and despite having a staple

00:19:43.429 --> 00:19:46.220
of characters that would absolutely carry
the franchise for another 20 years, maybe

00:19:46.220 --> 00:19:49.130
at this point, he's just like he's reached
a point in his career-

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.880
Screw it, yeah.
... where he's okay with just kind of, "Nah."

00:19:51.880 --> 00:19:53.730
He's just winging it now.

00:19:53.730 --> 00:19:56.420
It's just coasting for the next 25 years.

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:57.670
Doctor Bong.

00:19:57.670 --> 00:19:59.330
Here comes Doctor Bong.

00:19:59.330 --> 00:20:02.120
Doctor Bong is a Howard the Duck villain with
a bell for a head.

00:20:02.120 --> 00:20:03.840
You bet he is.

00:20:03.840 --> 00:20:05.713
I don't want to see that either.

00:20:05.713 --> 00:20:12.590
[crosstalk] one of the most untenable storylines
from the early 2000s, I want to say.

00:20:12.590 --> 00:20:16.390
Wait until you're not on your work computer
and go look it up.

00:20:16.390 --> 00:20:17.870
It's amazing.

00:20:17.870 --> 00:20:19.350
Oh man.

00:20:19.350 --> 00:20:25.730
So my pick for worst villain that they could
possibly introduce is another old, Fantastic

00:20:25.730 --> 00:20:27.750
Four villain.

00:20:27.750 --> 00:20:31.190
He goes by the Trapster, but his original
name...

00:20:31.190 --> 00:20:33.350
Tom, you look very excited.

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:35.450
You know who I'm talking about.

00:20:35.450 --> 00:20:36.659
Is it Paste-Pot Pete?

00:20:36.659 --> 00:20:37.669
It's Paste-Pot Pete.

00:20:37.669 --> 00:20:38.840
Paste-Pot Pete.

00:20:38.840 --> 00:20:42.270
I stumbled across Paste-Pot Pete as well.

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:47.900
Paste-Pot Pete carries a bucket of glue-
I bet he does.

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:53.380
... and he shoots the glue with his glue gun
and he fights the Human Torch and it's a close

00:20:53.380 --> 00:20:54.380
one.

00:20:54.380 --> 00:20:55.400
It's close.

00:20:55.400 --> 00:20:57.470
The Human Torch almost doesn't win.

00:20:57.470 --> 00:21:03.730
So Paste-Pot Pete is basically just like a
mom who shops at Marshalls for [crosstalk].

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:07.350
It's really good glue.

00:21:07.350 --> 00:21:08.400
It's really good.

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:09.820
They have glue at Marshalls.

00:21:09.820 --> 00:21:10.820
Right.

00:21:10.820 --> 00:21:15.810
I love the defense of Galactus was we're going
to bring in the Fantastic Four, but 25% of

00:21:15.810 --> 00:21:18.970
that team just almost got taken out by glue.

00:21:18.970 --> 00:21:20.260
By glue guy.

00:21:20.260 --> 00:21:23.240
It's fireproof glue, that's why.

00:21:23.240 --> 00:21:25.860
If it's fireproof, [crosstalk].

00:21:25.860 --> 00:21:26.860
I was being stupid.

00:21:26.860 --> 00:21:27.860
It was tough.

00:21:27.860 --> 00:21:28.860
It was tough.

00:21:28.860 --> 00:21:29.860
I was being stupid.

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:33.929
So the backstory of Paste-Pot Pete is apparently,
he was a brilliant scientist who developed

00:21:33.929 --> 00:21:37.460
a super duper effective, awesome glue.

00:21:37.460 --> 00:21:40.990
But instead of saying, "I should be in business.

00:21:40.990 --> 00:21:47.980
I should do things with my glue that are business-y,"
he says, "I'm going to Rob a bank and then

00:21:47.980 --> 00:21:51.409
I'm going to try to steal a missile."

00:21:51.409 --> 00:21:57.200
Luckily for the bank, the Human Torch was
online to access his savings account that

00:21:57.200 --> 00:21:58.200
day.

00:21:58.200 --> 00:22:04.210
So as it happened, the two of them tussled,
and after he defeated Paste-Pot Pete, he forever

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:09.730
harbored a grudge, excuse me, against the
Human Torch.

00:22:09.730 --> 00:22:10.730
There we go.

00:22:10.730 --> 00:22:13.130
Eventually, he changed his name to the Trapster.

00:22:13.130 --> 00:22:15.929
He still shoots glue out of his gloves.

00:22:15.929 --> 00:22:18.460
So he changed his name, not as gimmick.

00:22:18.460 --> 00:22:20.240
He was like, "This is working great, but [crosstalk].

00:22:20.240 --> 00:22:21.552
I think he does different traps.

00:22:21.552 --> 00:22:24.521
The problem isn't the glue.

00:22:24.521 --> 00:22:27.870
The problem is the appearance, the presentation.

00:22:27.870 --> 00:22:30.150
It's the branding.

00:22:30.150 --> 00:22:31.150
Right.

00:22:31.150 --> 00:22:35.820
Anyway, I feel like that would be maybe not
the best choice for MCU phase four.

00:22:35.820 --> 00:22:37.840
I would not want to see that.

00:22:37.840 --> 00:22:40.330
There's that.

00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:41.330
I love that.

00:22:41.330 --> 00:22:43.529
This is the Paste-Pot Pete.

00:22:43.529 --> 00:22:44.600
Thanks for joining us.

